codex
The first backend run exposed a real query bug: using SQLAlchemy’s bitwise `|` with the Python query flag produced the wrong predicate, so default listings returned no rows and archived rows leaked. I’m replacing it with an explicit conditional SQL predicate (`is false` unless the flag is enabled), then rerunning the focused Items tests before the full suite.
apply patch
